In a fictional world, the speed of light is c meters per second and the acceleration due to gravity is g meters per second squared.A 
person jumps from rest from a height H meters. During the fall, the relationship between the velocity v and the height descended is:
v^2 = 2 \times g \times H Find the minimum height (in meters) required for the person to reach the speed of light.
Input FormatA single line containing two space-separated integers: g cwhere: g is the acceleration due to gravity and c is the speed of light.
Output FormatPrint a single integer representing the minimum height required.




#include <iostream>
#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;

int main() {
    int g, c;
    cin >> g >> c;

    int h = (c * c) / (2 * g);

    cout << h;

    return 0;
}
